      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The patient encounter summary should be:\n\n\"65yo male presenting with dyspnea, palpitations, and orthopnea. May be experiencing angina with tight chest upon exertion, noting ankle edema. Vital signs: BP 155/95, HR 115; physical examination reveals bilateral ankle swelling, crackles in the lung bases. No previous history of myocardial infarction reported.\"\n\nThis summary includes 5 required coding terms (dyspnea, palpitations, orthopnea, angina, and edema) from the provided list. The coverage score would be (5/10).",
